From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zaid <283011337+nottzaid@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Compressed textures

ImageTexture reads BC7 and opaque BC1 from DDS files (mip levels
included) and uploads them as they are, with no CPU copy. Cached copies
of a compressed texture never regenerate mipmaps, which made the driver
decompress them (a 13 s stall). Decoded PNG textures are freed once
uploaded; infra-red distance sensors, the one later reader, reload the
file.

Replaces these patches of the numbered series, with what each measured
as it landed (tools/profile_forest.py, GTX 1060 3 GB, i5-4670):
- 0024-compressed-textures: GPU 2830 -> 2376 MB, RAM 2199 -> 1865 MB,
  frame 23.4 -> 22.5 ms
- 0054-texture-images-freed: RAM 1400 -> 1065 MB
- 0069-bc1-textures: the valley's land textures on the GPU: 3.5 MB; 7 MB
  as BC7, 28 MB as RGBA8
